# Synthetic artifact review

Approved AR13-01–05 only: source-bound fictional planning attestations in the dedicated localhost profile. Generated `FixPackageSnapshot`, artifact text, Unverified status and disclaimer remain unchanged. No execution, artifact editing, task/export, customer identity or production migration is provided.

`ArtifactReviewSourceBuilder` exports the exact dedicated profile/application/contract/template constants. It rebuilds actual guidance and packages, checks complete actual canonical bytes and cached digest/JSON, validates the thirteen locked fields, and retains the canonical package internally. Public historical source references contain metadata bindings and revision vectors, not package text. The server verifies retained historical full package bytes; clients cannot independently prove those historical bytes from references alone.

`SyntheticFixReviewStore` receives fixed scope and a request-scoped trusted source-reader callback. After opening a ReadCommitted transaction it acquires the shared run-wide transaction advisory fence, then invokes that callback exactly once. The callback must use fresh read-only owning-module APIs; never call seeding `DemoReviewService.ReadAsync` under this fence. Existing assessment/finding writers join the same fence before row/global locks. All callers must use the same guarded loopback `iga_synthetic_` database. The shared helper belongs to the coordinator, not this module.

Reads validate the complete current source, every immutable source version, all artifact identities and continuous event/receipt/current history. Current run revision and all finding revisions must dominate every recorded version; the same run revision and full finding vector cannot acquire a different source digest. A later run revision may change the digest with unchanged finding revisions. Reads write no source seed, receipt, invalidation event or current state.

Only the sole trusted Consultant role with exact assignment, Read/Review grants, Mutable state and full category visibility is accepted. Replay authority/current visibility/source validation precedes event lookup. Exact replay returns the original metadata receipt, including its historical timestamp/revision/source; it never restores the current overlay. New commands compare revision then full source digest, validate the transition and commit source registration, first artifact seed/current, event and receipt together. Latest review is ReviewedForPlanning only for the current full source; otherwise NeedsReview. Latest withdrawal stays Unverified across source changes.

Private semantic command digest: SHA256 of UTF8 compact JSON `{schemaVersion:"synthetic-fix-review-command-v1",scope,runId,artifactId,actorId,command:{eventId,kind,expectedRevision,expectedSourceDigest,reason}}`, recursively ordinal object keys, significant array order, web camelCase property names, default System.Text.Json escaping, lower-case D UUIDs and string enum values; no final newline. Reasons remain exact and are stored in JSON text so NUL can be escaped. Nonblank/max2000 UTF16 rules apply. Exact JSON string round-trip is additionally required: lone surrogates are denied instead of silently replaced; Unicode, NUL, CR/CRLF, tabs and leading/trailing spaces otherwise remain unchanged. Receipts exclude reasons/content and no reason/content is logged.

Migration001 is additive and owns only `synthetic_fix_review`. Exact embedded SQL digest, fixed scope and schema fingerprint are checked at initialization and every operation. Unexpected schema objects, drift, disabled guards or corrupt source/history fail closed. Immutable rows/events/receipts cannot be updated/deleted/truncated; current advances one revision matching an appended event, whose deferred commit guard requires receipt and current. Revision0 is initial; maximum9007199254740991 preserves HTTP integer fidelity. Rollback disables new profile/actions and retains append-only data; no down migration or purge exists.

Tests use independent literal canonical package/binding/artifact oracles authored before consuming module output. `tests/unit/SyntheticFixReview.Tests/run-checks.py` uses pinned SDK10.0.401, owned CLI cache, a minimal inherited environment and a disclosed test-only `DOTNET_hostBuilder__reloadConfigOnChange=false` workaround. It never configures production startup. PostgreSQL checks use optional explicit `IGA_A13_DATABASE` full connection configuration (default the owned local v2 database), require loopback `iga_synthetic_cycle13_` with trusted `iga_synthetic` role, preserve earlier run rows, and restore any bounded tamper/trigger before completion. Optional `IGA_A13_ORIGINAL_DATABASE` explicitly enables the read-only older-generation fingerprint case; absent configuration is NOT VERIFIED, never fabricated. The timestamp-precision probe runs only when the GLOBAL event table is empty; populated reruns skip it as NOT VERIFIED instead of rounding preserved history. Original failures and observed generations are retained separately from the final sealed source.
